# Reference illustration — DEPLOYMENT-ROOT secrets for the workspace topology.
#
# Two-tier .env model (docs/workspace.md → "Two-tier .env model"): the real
# per-repo secrets live in each child's own .env
# (widget/.env, gadget/.env — one GH_TOKEN + provider key each). This root file
# holds only what the SUPERVISOR itself needs: a token to install the shared git
# credential helper and to check the engine out. It is scrubbed out of every
# child engine's env (#61), so it is never the token a child pushes with — each
# child uses its own.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; only this `.example` is tracked.

# --- Required (supervisor: shared git credential helper + engine checkout) ---
GH_TOKEN=

# --- GitHub App arm (alternative to per-tenant GH_TOKEN) ---
# Set BOTH variables to have boot mint a per-tenant installation token from the
# App instead of reading each tenant's GH_TOKEN. App arm is available in both
# solo and workspace deployments.
# The private key must be base64-encoded as a single line:
#   Linux:  base64 -w0 your-app-key.pem
#   macOS:  base64 your-app-key.pem
# Never supply a file path — a mounted key file is readable by every tenant.
# PHOEBE_GH_APP_ID=
# PHOEBE_GH_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Fleet knobs (optional) ---
# Cap on concurrent work units across ALL children. 1 ⇒ children take turns.
# PHOEBE_MAX_CONCURRENT_AGENTS=1
# How often boot re-walks the workspace children + the shared engine ref.
# PHOEBE_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS=60000
